","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GET"},{"text":" response: the stored policy plus the unknown-AAGUID action it currently ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"resolves to","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unknown_aaguid"},{"text":" is nullable, where ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":" means “use this mode’s default” (deny under","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"direct_required"},{"text":", allow otherwise). A client that only saw the stored ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":" would have to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"re-derive that rule itself to display what the policy actually does — and a security rule","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"implemented twice is a security rule that will eventually disagree with itself. So the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"server resolves it once, here, and reports both: the admin’s stored intent and its effect.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/PolicyResponse","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PolicyResponse"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AttestationMode":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AttestationMode","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/attestationmode","title":"AttestationMode","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AttestationMode","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"What attestation conveyance a registration ceremony requests, and whether the policy is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enforced at all. ","type":"text"},{"code":"None","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the default and reproduces today’s behavior byte-for